1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,694
Your crush just texted back.

2
00:00:01,694 --> 00:00:03,459
Here's what your brain just did.

3
00:00:03,950 --> 00:00:06,519
Before you even open it, there's suspense.

4
00:00:06,519 --> 00:00:10,129
And your brain's reward chemical, dopamine, loves suspense.

5
00:00:10,429 --> 00:00:15,591
In one monkey study, dopamine cells stayed most active when a treat was fifty-fifty.

6
00:00:16,083 --> 00:00:17,511
Then you see their name.

7
00:00:17,511 --> 00:00:20,961
When scientists scanned people who were intensely in love,

8
00:00:20,961 --> 00:00:25,125
a photo of their person lit up the brain's dopamine-rich reward areas.

9
00:00:25,617 --> 00:00:27,790
Like and subscribe for more Crush Files.

10
00:00:28,090 --> 00:00:29,508
Now adrenaline kicks in.

11
00:00:29,508 --> 00:00:33,350
Your heart speeds up, and blood is pulled away from your stomach.

12
00:00:33,350 --> 00:00:34,473
Hello, butterflies.

13
00:00:34,983 --> 00:00:36,901
And rereading it ten times?

14
00:00:36,901 --> 00:00:43,434
One small study found people newly in love had serotonin changes a lot like people with OCD.

15
00:00:43,950 --> 00:00:45,668
Your whole brain just reacted.

16
00:00:45,668 --> 00:00:47,501
More Crush Files on the channel.
